<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Fisk University Jubilee Quartet (Victor 16453)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1909</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording, the first gospel song to sell a million copies</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Paul Robeson (Victor 20068)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1926</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Everybody Sing (film; Judy Garland in blackface)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1938</span><span class="sg-chain-h">swing version with special lyrics</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Joan Baez at Woodstock</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">performance</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Swing Low, Sweet Cadillac (Dizzy Gillespie)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1951; 1967</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Eric Clapton, There's One in Every Crowd</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1975</span><span class="sg-chain-h">reggae version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Sheep (Pink Floyd, Roger Waters)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1977</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Bravery of Being Out of Range (Roger Waters)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1992</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Union featuring the England World Cup Squad</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1991</span><span class="sg-chain-h">rugby World Cup single</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">China Black with Ladysmith Black Mambazo</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1995</span><span class="sg-chain-h">rugby World Cup single</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">UB40 and the United Colours of Sound</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">rugby World Cup single</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ella Eyre</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2015</span><span class="sg-chain-h">rugby World Cup single</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">2 Kings 2:11 (Elijah taken up in a chariot)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the image</span></li></ul></section>
